+# Incidents brief, August–September 2026
+
+Follow-up status as of the 30 September on-call meeting.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall, full database disk
+
+- **Impact:** data processing stopped overnight for about 2.5 hours; customers saw stale dashboards. No data lost.
+- **Root cause:** a malformed batch jammed ingest, which retried it endlessly; the retry logs filled the database disk, halting writes.
+- **Fix:** restarted ingest with the bad batch set aside, then cleaned up the database and old logs.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Disk alert at 80% (Sunil): done.
+  - Stop bad batches jamming ingest (Jonas): open, in review.
+  - Paging escalation review (no owner named): done; unanswered pages escalate after 15 minutes.
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+- **Impact:** public API down for 47 minutes (08:05–08:52), failing nearly every client.
+- **Root cause:** the API's certificate expired; its automatic renewal had silently failed for three weeks on an outdated access token.
+- **Fix:** renewed the certificate, restarted the API; renewal failures now raise an alert.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Reminder 14 days before each expiry (Priya): done.
+  - Alert on days left (Priya): open.
+  - Expiry check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open.
+  - Responders record actions during incidents (Mara): done.
